To ensure the Collaborative Session chat **never** opens unless a partner is confirmed (even when navigating away and coming back), I will modify the `CollaborativeSession.tsx` component.

The key fix is in the `useEffect` hook that listens to the session data. Instead of only checking if we *were* verifying, I will now **strictly enforce** the lock state based on the participant count every time the data updates. If there are fewer than 2 participants, the app will force the "Waiting" screen, regardless of previous state.

I will also ensure that when a session is selected or loaded, it *starts* in the locked state by default until Firestore confirms the participant count.

