To ensure the Collaborative Session chat strictly adheres to the pairing logic—meaning it **never** opens unless a partner is confirmed to be in the session (even after navigating away and returning)—I will update `components/CollaborativeSession.tsx`.

I will implement a **Strict Enforcement** policy within the Firestore real-time listener. Every time the session data updates (or loads for the first time), the app will check the participant count. If there are fewer than 2 participants, it will force the "Waiting" overlay, regardless of any previous state.

I will also ensure that when a session is restored from navigation (`activeCode`), it defaults to the "Verifying" state immediately to prevent any flash of unverified content before the data loads.

