To fix the issue where the session opens freely due to "ghost" participants (users who left but weren't cleared) and to ensure strict, real-time pairing, I will implement a **Heartbeat Presence System**.

**How it works:**
1.  **Heartbeat**: Every 10 seconds, your app updates a timestamp in the database (`activeParticipants.{username}: Date.now()`).
2.  **Strict Check**: The chat **only** unlocks if it sees at least 2 participants with timestamps from the last 60 seconds.
3.  **Auto-Relock**: If your partner leaves or closes the app, their timestamp expires, and the chat locks again ("Waiting for partner...") automatically.

This ensures the "Waiting" screen is accurate and prevents the chat from opening if the other person isn't actually there live.

